docs/phase-1-plan.md:29:| 2 | `schwab_tokens` | `access_token` (encrypted), `refresh_token` (encrypted), `access_expires_at`, `refresh_expires_at` (= `issued_at` + 168 hours, never moved by access refreshes), `issued_at`, `last_refreshed_at`, `last_refresh_error`, `revoked_at`, `scope` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:34:| 7 | `orders` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `broker_order_id` (unique per account), `status` enum incl. Phase 2 states, `side`, `quantity`, `filled_quantity`, `order_type`, `limit_price`, `stop_price`, `remaining_quantity`, `strategy_type` (SINGLE/TRIGGER/OCO, reconciliation needs it), `duration`, `session`, `tax_lot_method`, `placed_via` enum (schwab_direct/app), `parent_order_id` (self FK, bracket child), `replaces_order_id` (self FK, cancel/replace chain), `order_proposal_id` (nullable), `entered_at`, `closed_at`, `raw` jsonb. `instrument_id` is nullable for container strategies with no legs. Index on (account, instrument, entered_at) for Phase 2 reconciliation. An upsert never nulls a lineage or proposal column that already has a value | yes (sync only) |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:35:| 8 | `order_proposals` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `kind` enum (entry, exit, stop_adjustment), `target_order_id` (nullable, for stop adjustments), `origin` enum (agent/human), `user_id` (nullable), `status` enum (proposed, validated, rejected, approved, submitted, submission_unknown, filled, cancelled), `side`, `quantity`, `order_type`, `limit_price`, `stop_price` (the order's own trigger), `planned_stop` (the protective stop that becomes the bracket child), `target_price`, `duration`, `session`, `tax_lot_method`, `thesis`, `setup_id`, `guardrail_results` jsonb (records `{rule_id, version}` pairs), `acknowledged_warnings` jsonb, `expires_at`, `override_reason`, `reject_reason`, `approved_at`, `submitted_at` | no |
