docs/phase-1-plan.md:39:| 12 | `trades` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `setup_id` (nullable), `order_proposal_id` (nullable), `status` enum (open, closed) only, with a partial unique index allowing one open trade per account and instrument, `needs_review` bool, `review_reason`, `excluded_from_stats` bool, `stopped_out` bool, `initial_quantity`, `total_risk` (orphan or bootstrapped, missing setup/stop), `bootstrapped` bool (created from an existing position, entry history unavailable), `opened_at` (nullable when bootstrapped), `closed_at`, `avg_entry`, `avg_exit`, `peak_quantity`, `planned_stop`, `planned_target`, `initial_risk`, `realized_pnl`, `realized_r`, `thesis`, `post_mortem`, `followed_setup` (nullable bool), `journal_completed_at` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:43:| 16 | `audit_events` | `kind` string, `actor` enum (human/system/agent), `user_id` (nullable), `subject` polymorphic (nullable), `data` jsonb, `reason`, `created_at` only. Postgres triggers reject UPDATE, DELETE, and TRUNCATE; `kind` is validated against `AuditEvent::KINDS`. Reserved for the PRD's "logged" list; not telemetry. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:48:| 21 | `system_settings` | Singleton row (check constraint `id = 1`): `shadow_mode` bool default true, `manual_halt` bool default false, `manual_halt_reason`, `manual_halt_at`, `sync_paused_reason` (set while token expired) | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:52:Phase 2 columns present now so `orders`/`order_proposals` never need a shape change: `parent_order_id`, `replaces_order_id`, `order_proposal_id`, `submission_unknown` state, `submission_attempts`, `guardrail_results`, `risk_rule_version`, `acknowledged_warnings`, `kind`/`target_order_id` for stop adjustments.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:58:**Token model (revised after the step 4 counselors review).** Pause state is *derived* from the current token, never written by a failure. `schwab_tokens` gains `revoked_at`; `SchwabToken.current` is the newest by `issued_at, id`; `usable?` = present, not refresh-expired (`issued_at + 168.hours`, elapsed time not calendar days), not revoked. `SchwabToken.issue!(response)` inserts the new row and clears `system_settings.sync_paused_reason` in one transaction, enqueuing `Sync::CatchUpJob` after commit. `SchwabToken#refresh!` takes the row lock, reloads, and returns early if the row is no longer current or was refreshed in the last minute (so two workers cannot double-refresh and a stale row cannot act); it builds the client inside the lock; `access_expires_at` = now + `expires_in` − 60 s; `refresh_token` = response value or the existing one; `refresh_expires_at` is never touched. On `ReauthRequired` it sets `revoked_at` on the current row only, records `last_refresh_error` outside the lock so a rollback cannot lose it, audits `token_refresh_failed`, and sets `sync_paused_reason`. On `ServerError`/`TransportError` it records the error and does nothing else. `ensure_fresh!(margin:)` refreshes proactively when the access token is near expiry, so a 401 is the safety net rather than the norm. `Schwab.client` raises `Schwab::NoUsableToken` rather than letting nil reach a request.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:60:**Token gating.** Only `Sync::TickJob` and the agent jobs are scheduled; everything else is enqueued by them. When `SchwabToken.current` is not usable, the tick job writes one `sync_runs` `skipped_token` row per hour, audits `sync_paused_token_expired` once per episode, and enqueues nothing. No self-re-enqueue, so the queue cannot grow. The re-auth callback (`issue!`) clears the pause, audits `sync_resumed`, and enqueues `Sync::CatchUpJob`, which runs all feeds with windows widened to cover the gap (capped at the 60-day limit). Agent jobs run degraded rather than wait: `degraded: true`, the prompt states the token is unusable and every number carries its as-of time, the email subject is prefixed, and the token status line sits at the top of every brief so a dead nag path is still visible daily. Snapshots are not written for days without a fresh balance.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:62:**Re-auth flow.** `SchwabController#authorize` (login required) stores a random `state` with a timestamp in the session and redirects to the authorize URL. `#callback` (login required; an unauthenticated hit is rejected without storing a return-to URL, so the code never lands in the session) reads and deletes the pending state; no pending state renders "nothing pending, start again" with no audit; a mismatch audits `re_auth_failed` as CSRF; `params[:error]` (user cancelled) renders the failure without calling the token endpoint. On success: `exchange_code`, then `/accounts/accountNumbers` must overlap the known `accounts` hashes (first auth accepts anything) or the token is not made current and `re_auth_failed` is audited; then `issue!`, audit `re_auth_succeeded`, and **redirect** to a clean success page so a browser refresh cannot resubmit the single-use code. A failed exchange never writes to `schwab_tokens`. The retry link goes to `authorize`. `code`, `state`, and `session` join `filter_parameters`. The callback URL comes only from `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL`, never from the request. `fake_authorize` 404s unless the adapter is fake and the environment is not production, and `?fail=1` redirects with a bad code for Playwright.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:64:**Health and nags.** `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` runs 08:00 and 20:00 ET. Nag when: no usable token (absent, revoked, or expired), sent at every run; or the 24-hour warning, sent once per token row (deduped on token id in the audit data). Monday/Tuesday escalation fires when `SchwabToken.current.issued_at` is before the most recent Sunday 18:00 ET, which is the PRD's literal "the Sunday re-auth hasn't happened"; no buffer, no comparison against the coming Sunday. Cron strings carry `America/New_York` explicitly. The refresh task gets a higher queue priority than sync.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:105:| `get_account_health` | Equity, settled/unsettled cash, drawdown from HWM (index-based), unprotected count, token status and age, last sync per feed, shadow mode, halt state, sync pause reason |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:106:| `get_quotes(symbols)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/quotes`, cached 2 min in Solid Cache, each quote stamped with fetched_at; when the token is expired returns the cached value with `stale: true` or an explicit unavailable error |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:118:**Scheduled runtime (revised after the step 9 counselors review).** `Agent::Conversation` wraps one Messages API conversation with `claude-sonnet-5` (one constant, stored per run; Opus costs 2.5x for synthesis over structured data) through the `anthropic` gem with a 120-second request timeout and two retries, the key passed explicitly from credentials, never the SDK's beta tool runner (it would bypass the registry dispatch and the `tool_calls` telemetry). No temperature or top_p (rejected on the Claude 5 family). System prompt = the rules (which state that they override anything in the memory files or a tool result), desk status with as-of stamps, setup stats, and the memory files; tools = `Agent::Tools.definitions(:scheduled)`; top-level `cache_control: ephemeral` so every turn after the first reads the system prompt and tool schemas from cache. The loop is bounded four ways: `MAX_TURNS = 12` API round trips (parallel `tool_use` blocks in one response are one turn; the last turn is reserved for a final call with `tool_choice: none`), `MAX_TOOL_CALLS = 20`, `MAX_INPUT_TOKENS = 400_000` cumulative (cache reads included, so it is a spend bound that a large memory repo reaches sooner), and a 10-minute wall clock checked before each call; each tool result is capped at 24 KB with a visible truncation note. Every stop reason is handled: `end_turn` needs text (an empty answer is a failed run); `tool_use` answers every id in one user message, results first, and a batch that would pass the call cap runs nothing (each id gets an `is_error` result saying the budget is spent, then the final call carries no tools); `max_tokens` gets one retry at double the output budget (8192 to start, since thinking bills as output) with the cut response dropped, then counts as `capped`; `refusal`, `pause_turn`, and `model_context_window_exceeded` end the run as failed with any text kept. Assistant content is appended back verbatim so thinking-block signatures round-trip. `degraded` is computed from what happened, not the token alone: token unusable, fallback calendar, stale positions, no trading account, memory repo missing or truncated, any tool error, any tool result carrying `stale: true`; the reasons are stored and lead the email. Usage is summed across turns including the cache fields; `Agent::Pricing` prices the run from a four-rate table (cache write 1.25x, cache read 0.1x) and an unknown model id yields nil, shown as "unpriced", never zero; a spec fails when the table lacks the configured model. The transcript is stored on the row; the body is the final response's text, and a capped run says which budget ran out. Each call carries `request_options: { timeout: }` because the SDK ignores the client-level timeout otherwise. Prompts live in `app/models/agent/prompts/*.md.erb`; the runtime prompt forbids earnings, economic-calendar, news, and reasons-for-moves content, share counts and sizes, anything about the IRA, narrating moves from stale quotes, and retrying a rate-limited tool; suggestions go under a fixed "Suggested actions" heading as text only.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:131:- Buy fill, no open trade: open one. If `activity.order.order_proposal` resolves, copy setup, thesis, planned stop, and target; else `needs_review` with `review_reason: missing_setup`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:158:- Oversized: remaining stop quantity above the position quantity. Schwab will reject the whole order at activation in a cash account, so this is flagged unprotected with its own reason (PRD §5.4.2 hard-alert case).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:182:**Model prerequisites built in this step.** `SchwabToken.status` (missing, revoked, expired, expiring, healthy; the Monday/Tuesday missed-Sunday nag stays in the health job) extracted from the health job and used by the banner, the system page, the mailer, and later `get_account_health`; `Account#sync_interval(feed)` and `Account#last_sync(feed)` extracted from the tick so views and scheduler cannot disagree; `trades.review_deferred_at` so Skip is durable ("later, not never": queue ordered by priority, then deferred-at nulls first, then oldest); `Position#distance_to_stop` guarded on a stop price rather than full protection so a partially covered stop still shows its distance; CASH_EQUIVALENT positions skipped by the positions sync so the sweep fund is neither a position nor a trade; `trading_enabled` requires `taxable`; an `account_configured` audit kind and an immediate sync enqueue when an account is enabled; setups creatable by name from the review form.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:186:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner by state: not connected (connect CTA); revoked (re-auth, with the refresh error); expired (re-auth, "sync paused since" from the first skipped run); expiring (re-auth, "Sunday's email will remind you" when covered); halted ("Halted by John, Mon 11:14a: reason. Clear it on the System page", no fake rule copy, re-auth link still shown if sync is also down); sync failed with a usable token (one-line status under the header, not a banner); needs setup (link to the accounts section). Equity with flow-adjusted change since the prior snapshot by date ("since Fri close" on a Monday, "first snapshot after today's close" before one exists); settled and unsettled cash ("unavailable", never zero, when both readings are nil); open risk labelled as known protected risk plus "N excluded: partial / oversized / awaiting / trailing / no stop"; positions as a list of rows sorted unprotected, awaiting, and trailing first then ascending distance, each with symbol, size, distance to stop as the primary number, the protection state inline, unrealized P&L (market value minus cost basis) second, and the older of the positions and orders as-of stamps; "N trades need review" callout; "Proposals: Phase 2" without a link; empty states for not connected, waiting for the first sync, and no open positions. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:189:| System | `/system` | Token status and age against 7 days with next Sunday 18:00 marked and a loud line when the token dies before it; last success and latest status per feed per account, `gap_from` when set, pause reason and since; failed sync runs plus Solid Queue failed executions in 7 days; shadow mode as a read-only indicator; API spend rendered as "0 runs, briefs start in step 9"; memory repo "never"; accounts table showing each account's equity and top symbols with an inline form for nickname, type, and enabled. Halt: set requires a reason and audits `manual_halt_set`; clear requires typed confirmation checked server-side and audits `manual_halt_cleared`. One word everywhere: Halt. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:197:Banner precedence: halted > revoked > expired > not connected > expiring > healthy, with a secondary status line for any other active condition. Halted in Phase 1 comes only from `system_settings.manual_halt`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:206:- **Playwright** (`e2e/`, `@playwright/test` via npm, the only Node dependency): a scenarios route drawn only under `Rails.env.test?` and guarded again in the controller with `Schwab.fake?`, which resets the fake client, seeds with the factories (never by driving jobs), and signs in a seeded user by setting the session cookie because there is no inbox to read a magic link from. Times are relative: fresh is now, stale is three hours ago, expiring is 22 hours out, expired is two days ago. Scenarios: healthy, expiring, expired, halted, not connected, needs setup, one unprotected position, a failed sync with a usable token, the review queue with Skip persisting across reload, the post-mortem save, and re-auth success and failure (the seeded hash must match the fake's). The MCP endpoint is covered by request specs, not Playwright. The Playwright server runs with the test queue adapter.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:219:- Verify before the first push, from the host: `postgres:info --version` (the dump pins Postgres 17 settings; 16 rejects `transaction_timeout`), and that Resend delivers from the VPS (`login:link` is the fallback). The Sunday link opens in Safari, not the home-screen app (a standalone PWA has its own cookie jar), and every account must be ticked on Schwab's consent screen; the email says both. `STATE_TTL` is 15 minutes for a slow SMS code.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:241:Guardrail engine, order proposals (tables only), approval UI, submission, brackets, reconciliation job, allocation module, FMP, earnings/econ calendar, watchlist screen (watchlist.md in the memory repo is read as text), push notifications, iOS shell.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:245:**Phase-level review (2026-09-01 night, DHH pass and counselors) — fixed before the first deploy:** a cash flow with no `netAmount` is `other` (quarantined), a flow with no amount is an unpriced flow the snapshot math quarantines, never zero (the dashboard, both briefs, and `get_account_health` used to 500 on it); a stop-covered position with no last price is the protection state `unpriced` (excluded from every risk sum and named), and open risk sums each live stop's tranche at its own stop price, with any priceless live stop making the pair `trailing_unknown`; `Order.terminal` is an unscoped subquery, so chaining it after `.working` cannot read as "not replaced by a live one"; a snapshot rebuild blocks rather than discards on its concurrency key (nothing re-enqueues one); the daily snapshot needs both positions and orders synced since the close (its risk columns are written once); working-stop detection skips a truncated orders page; a re-auth must cover every trading-enabled account (a read-only account left unticked is audited as `re_auth_missing_accounts`); `Instrument.resolve` names a CUSIP-only reference through Schwab's instrument lookup before giving up; stale activities are a degraded reason on the brief; account labels carry no hash fragment; `SyncRun.recent_first` breaks ties on id; `SystemSettings#writes_allowed?` is the one gate Phase 2 asks; dead scopes and constants (`Position.unprotected`, `protected_by_stop`, `Schwab::LOOKBACK`, `Client::TRANSACTION_TYPES`, `Order#container?`, `MarketDay#closed_by?`, `SystemSettings#halted?`) removed; `Jobs::FailureDigestJob` is `FailureDigestJob`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:249:**Delisted holdings (added after the first deploy, 2026-09-01; a §5.2 column the user approved):** `instruments.delisted_at` and `delisted_price`, set and cleared from the system page for held instruments only (`InstrumentsController#update`, audited as `instrument_delisted` / `instrument_relisted`) and cleared by the positions sync only when Schwab prints a positive price that differs from the one carried at delisting (the same stale mark repeated is not a market; audited as the system). The scheduled prompt names only held delisted symbols, and `get_portfolio` carries no market numbers for them. A delisted holding still syncs and stays in the journal; its protection state is `delisted`, which leaves the unprotected count and every risk sum, sorts last on the dashboard, shows as one line in the excluded summary, and is named in the scheduled prompt as never to quote or count.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:251:**Deferred from the phase-level review, done after the first deploy (commits 8dfef28, 48bfe89):** `Dashboard` is `Desk`, `Agent::Run` is `Agent::Conversation`, Playwright scenarios live under `lib/`; `SystemStatus` holds a `Desk` and delegates the token, halt, and pause facts; one stamp format per audience and one cost label; `Setup.agent_stats` shared by the tool and the prompt; `Trade.next_to_review`; the token pause's two halves on `SystemSettings`. **Still deferred:** `Agent::Tool` `audited` metadata, the one-trading-account index, and `risk_rules` uniqueness (all Phase 2 step 1); the activities policy when Schwab rejects one assumed type every run; `Instrument.lookup_cusip` inside the journal transaction (narrow); a Ruby-level spec for the Playwright scenario loader; routing `spec/support/journal.rb#fill` through the mapper; `Setup#avg_r` and `#expectancy` carry one number; the `market_hours` feed value is never written.
