docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:9:1. **Push/email notification** → deep link to a specific proposal, trade, or health alert. This is the primary mobile entry.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:18:| Proposal detail | **Mobile-first** | The approve/reject decision |
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:19:| Proposal queue | Mobile + desktop | List of pending/recent proposals |
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:20:| New proposal (manual) | Mobile + desktop | Human-initiated order proposal |
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:35:- **Token expired:** sync paused. Everything shows "as of [timestamp]" staleness marks. Re-auth is the only call to action.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:36:- **Halted:** daily-loss or drawdown rule tripped. Banner states which rule and when it resets. New-proposal entry points disabled, exits still available.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:38:Dashboard content: equity + day change, open positions (each: symbol, size, unrealized P&L, distance to stop as the primary number), total open risk ($ and % of equity), settled vs unsettled cash, pending proposal count (links to queue).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:42:## Flow 2: Review and approve a proposal (mobile-first, the core flow)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:54:- **Warn(s) present** (e.g., wash-sale flag): approve is available but each warning must be individually acknowledged first (tap to expand and acknowledge).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:55:- **Stop outside collar:** approve gated behind a required typed reason (logged). Show the collar bounds and where the stop sits.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:56:- **Hard fail** (GFV, notional cap, halt active): no approve control at all. The failing rule is stated with its numbers. Only actions: reject, or edit-and-resubmit (which creates a new proposal through the same validation).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:57:- **Approved → submitted → filled/cancelled:** read-only timeline view. Fill pushes a notification and links to the new journal row.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:59:Reject: optional one-line reason, stored on the proposal.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:61:## Flow 3: Manual proposal (human-initiated)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:63:**New proposal** form: symbol → live quote loads → entry, stop, target fields.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:70:Submit → same validation path and proposal detail screen as Flow 2. Human and agent proposals are identical objects downstream; the only difference is the author field.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:91:No bulk edit. No editing while a halt is active (prevents mood-driven loosening on a bad day; the halt banner says so).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:99:Token age (days:hours, with the Sunday cadence marked), last successful sync per feed, recent job failures, API spend this month. One control: **Pause system** (kill switch): stops all proposal creation and submission until unpaused. Unpause requires typed confirmation.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:105:- **Token expired:** global banner, read-only mode for anything requiring fresh Schwab data.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:110:Push (deep-link only, no figures in the payload): new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, unprotected position, token expiring. Email: morning brief, EOD summary, Sunday ritual, job-failure digests. Original list:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:113:- New proposal awaiting review
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:114:- Fill / cancel on a submitted order
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:115:- Guardrail halt tripped
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:128:- **Home → Dashboard.** Balance hero with a 30-day sparkline, accounts card to the right, a paired "money in / money out" block below, and a quick-action pill row under the greeting. Our mapping: equity + equity curve as the hero, positions as the side card, "open risk / settled cash" as the pair, and "pending proposals" as the first pill.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:129:- **Transaction detail slide-over → Proposal detail.** Amount hero at top, then a vertical timeline (source → destination with timestamps), then metadata fields, then notes/attachments/comments. Our order is the same: order hero, thesis, guardrail rows where Mercury has GL code and notes, timeline once approved. On desktop the proposal opens as a right-hand panel over the queue, as Mercury does; on mobile it is the full screen.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:132:- **"A similar payment has been created" callout → duplicate and warn states.** Mercury surfaces a possible duplicate inline in the form with the prior item embedded. Same component serves the wash-sale warn-acknowledge and the `submission_unknown` reconciliation notice.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:133:- **Status pills in rows** (Pending, Failed) → proposal states in the queue and `unprotected` on positions.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:140:- **Midday (web) → app shell and dashboard.** Icon-only collapsed left rail (~40px) with a top search bar; dark theme; chart cards with a headline number, legend (current / previous / average), dashed average line, and a timeframe dropdown plus "Customize" at the card row's top right. Layout: one full-width primary chart, then a 2-up row of smaller chart cards. Our mapping: equity curve as the primary chart with HWM as the dashed line; the 2-up row is open risk over time and drawdown from HWM. The rail holds our five areas: dashboard, proposals, journal, watchlist, system.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:141:- **Mercury (web) → detail panel, journal table, confirm pattern.** Unchanged from the section above: right-hand slide-over for proposal detail, transactions table for the journal, authorization-line-above-one-button for Approve, inline "similar item exists" callout for warn and reconciliation states.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:142:- **Copilot Money (web), supplemental.** Three cards worth lifting: "Transactions to review" with its reviewed-everything empty state (our proposal queue on the dashboard), the range-chip row (1W / 1M / 3M / YTD / 1Y / ALL) on the net-worth chart, and "Next two weeks" as a dated upcoming list (our earnings/econ events touching the book).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:143:- **Mobile supplements (iOS).** Revolut Business approval detail for the proposal screen structure; Navan's in-policy / out-of-policy idiom for pass/warn/fail rows and the override-with-reason sentence; Life Reset's Quick Add for the journal entry.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:145:Open interaction with the earlier question: a dark shell makes "halt mutes the whole palette" a weaker signal than on a light UI; the halt banner probably has to carry the state on its own.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:152:- **Holding detail page.** Price chart with range chips, a "Your position" strip (balance, shares, cost basis, return, allocation), then a right-column card with News / About tabs and a stats row below. This is our **Position detail** screen, which the inventory above omits. Our version of the strip: shares, cost basis, unrealized P&L, working stop, distance to stop, this position's share of open risk. Right column tabs become Thesis (from the originating proposal) and History (journal legs for this instrument).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:160:**Monarch** is not on Mobbin. Worth screenshotting directly for the board: its transactions "needs review" queue and the net worth / holdings views are the closest consumer analogues to our proposal queue and dashboard.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:170:**Guardrail headroom as budget bars.** Budget card rows (label, planned amount right-aligned, progress bar, spent left / remaining right in green). Direct lift for a "Risk budget" card on the dashboard: risk-per-trade used, daily loss used vs halt threshold, sector exposure vs cap, concurrent positions vs max. Remaining headroom in green; the bar goes to the warn color as it approaches the cap. This makes the guardrail engine visible before a proposal trips it.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:172:**Review modal → orphan-fill and incomplete-journal review.** "Is this merchant recurring? There are 9 more to review": entity card with recent transactions, a few form fields, and three actions (Skip / Not recurring / Save as recurring). Ours: "Is this fill part of a setup? N more to review", recent fills for the instrument, setup dropdown and planned stop, actions Skip / Not a trade / Save. The orange top banner with "Review now" is the pending-review entry point; the nav badge count (Recurring 10) is the proposals count on the rail.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:180:**AI-origin marker.** Monarch marks AI-generated content with a sparkle glyph next to the title (Weekly Recap, Budget, Spending). Adopt it: every agent-authored element (thesis, brief, review suggestion) carries the glyph, so human vs agent origin is legible at a glance. Ties to the origin field on proposals.
spec/requests/system_spec.rb:16:  it "halts with a reason and resumes with a typed confirmation, auditing both, and refuses to resume when not halted" do
