docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:9:A personal investment operating system for a Schwab taxable brokerage account. A Rails application acts as the system of record and the sole gateway to Schwab's Trader API. Claude acts as the analysis and workflow agent on top of it, via an MCP server the Rails app exposes. The human approves every order.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:19:- Human-in-the-loop order flow: agent proposes, Rails validates, human approves, Rails submits.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:25:- Options strategies beyond the account's approved option level.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:40:│ memory files │                      │  - Order proposal queue  │
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:58:- **OAuth:** three-legged OAuth 2.0. Access token ~30 min, refresh token hard-expires at 7 days with no programmatic renewal.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:63:- **Client generation:** the api-evangelist OpenAPI specs turned out to be skeletal (minimal order schema, no response schemas for chains), so treat them as scaffolding only. Better references for the real shapes: the schwab-py order-builder docs and community client libraries that model the full schema; replace with Schwab's official schemas once portal access is approved. Wrap in a thin service layer with retry/backoff and rate-limit awareness.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:65:- **Order submission idempotency:** the Schwab order POST has no client-supplied order id (per community clients; confirm post-approval), so dedupe is local. The approved → submitted transition runs under a row lock and is the only code path that can call the order endpoint. On an ambiguous outcome (timeout, 5xx, connection drop after send), the proposal enters `submission_unknown`; a reconciliation job queries the orders endpoint for a matching order (instrument, qty, side, price, time window) before any retry. No blind retries, ever.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:73:- `order_proposals` (agent- or human-initiated; status: proposed → validated/rejected → approved → submitted → filled/cancelled; stores guardrail evaluation results as JSON; carries a submission_attempt record for the ambiguous-outcome path in 5.1)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:75:- `trades` (journal). A trade is one instrument's position lifecycle from zero back to zero; scale-ins and scale-outs are `trade_legs` linked to transactions. Fields: setup tag, thesis, planned stop/target, realized R-multiple, post_mortem. Fills with no originating proposal (orders placed at Schwab directly) create a trade in `incomplete` state with no planned stop; the EOD brief asks for the missing stop/setup rather than computing a bogus R.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:79:- `audit_events` (append-only: approvals, rejections, collar overrides with reason, rule edits with before/after, kill-switch toggles, re-auths, shadow-mode toggles). Every mention of "logged" elsewhere in this doc means a row here.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:91:Rules stored as data, evaluated server-side against every `order_proposal`. Every evaluation is logged with pass/fail per rule. Starting set:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:95:3. Daily loss halt and max-drawdown halt (blocks new proposals, not exits).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:96:4. **Account-type specific (decided: cash account):** settled-cash check before any buy. Source of truth is the balances endpoint (settled cash / cash available for trading), not a local settlement ledger; the app only projects the effect of pending approved proposals on top of the broker figure. Rule is deliberately the conservative form: a buy must be fully covered by settled cash. (Buying with unsettled funds is legal if you don't sell before settlement; that path is intentionally not supported in v1 because it creates a second, time-dependent constraint on exits.) No shorting, no margin order types. PDT counter not needed.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:102:8. **Stop collar (see 5.4.1):** every entry proposal must include a stop, and the stop must fall within the computed collar or the proposal is flagged for override.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:122:- A stop outside the collar does not hard-block; it requires an explicit human override with a logged reason. (Guardrails 1-7 remain hard blocks where marked.)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:126:- Nightly job recomputes Chandelier/ATR trails for open positions. Where the recomputed trail is tighter than the working stop, the EOD brief surfaces a "tighten stop" suggestion with the numbers. Adjusting the actual stop order remains a human-approved action (Phase 3 candidate for auto-submit of tighten-only adjustments).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:132:An app-only stop with 5-15 minute polling is not protection. Every approved entry is submitted as a bracket: the entry order with a one-triggers-another child stop order (Schwab order strategies support this; confirm exact strategy type names post-approval). Consequences:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:135:- "Tighten stop" is a cancel/replace of the child order, which goes through the proposal pipeline as a stop-adjustment proposal (guardrails: new stop must be tighter than current for the Phase 3 auto-submit class; any loosening is human-only with a logged reason).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:149:- `propose_order(params, thesis, setup)` → creates order_proposal, runs guardrails, returns evaluation
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:153:Explicitly absent from MCP: submit_order, cancel_order, edit_risk_rules, token operations. Submission happens only in the Rails approval UI (or a signed confirmation link), by the human.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:159:- **Interactive (human present):** the Claude app (desktop/Cowork/web) with the Rails MCP server registered as a remote connector. Rails exposes MCP over HTTPS with bearer-token auth (token in dokku config, rotatable). This is where ad hoc analysis, screening, and order proposals happen, billed through the Claude subscription seat.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:160:- **Scheduled (unattended):** Solid Queue jobs on the VPS call the Anthropic Messages API directly with an API key, passing tool definitions that map to the same internal service layer the MCP server uses (in-process, no MCP hop). Output is rendered to email. This covers the 07:00 brief, 16:30 EOD, and Sunday review. **Unattended runs get read-only tools only.** These runs ingest untrusted text (transcripts, news, fetched pages), so `propose_order`, `add_watchlist_item`, and `annotate_trade` are not in their tool set; anything a brief wants to suggest is rendered as text in the email, and the human creates the proposal interactively. Write tools exist only in the interactive runtime. Each scheduled job also has a hard cap on tool turns. Rationale: unattended runs can't depend on a desktop app being open, and keeping the scheduler in Rails means the VPS is the single ops surface (one place for cron, retries, failure alerts, and the token-health gate).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:183:Mobile is in scope: everything renders on a phone; proposal detail, dashboard glance, and journal quick-entry are mobile-first. Full screen inventory, flows, and per-screen states live in the companion doc `investment-copilot-ui-flows.md`; John designs against that. Summary:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:185:- Dashboard (glance, with healthy/expiring/expired/halted banner states)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:186:- Proposal queue + proposal detail (the approve/reject decision; deliberate-confirm on approve; warn-acknowledge, collar-override-with-reason, and hard-fail states)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:187:- Manual proposal form with live collar + auto-sizing feedback
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:190:- Risk rule editor (desktop-only, effect preview, versioned, locked during halts; override path exists: engage the kill switch, type a reason, then edit, so a misconfigured rule that caused a false halt can be fixed without waiting for reset)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:196:- **What the native shell adds:** APNs push, Face ID / device passcode as the deliberate confirm on Approve (resolves the open question in the flows doc: the second gesture is biometric, not a slide), app icon and home-screen presence, native navigation stack. Path configuration marks proposal detail, dashboard, and journal entry as the mobile-first routes.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:197:- **Notifications, revised:** time-sensitive alerts move from email to push once the app exists: new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, `unprotected` position, token expiring. Briefs and the Sunday ritual stay email (long-form, read on a desktop anyway). Push payloads carry no financial figures; they deep-link and the app fetches.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:198:- **Distribution:** TestFlight internal testing (no beta review for internal testers; builds expire after 90 days, so the CI pipeline produces a fresh build on a cadence) or direct dev-signed install from Xcode. TestFlight is the default; direct install is the fallback if the developer account state makes TestFlight awkward.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:209:- **Shadow mode (Schwab has no sandbox):** a global flag, on by default in production until deliberately turned off. In shadow mode the entire pipeline runs, including human approval, but the submission step writes a `would_have_submitted` audit event and the order payload instead of calling Schwab. Playwright runs in shadow mode. Phase 2 ships with shadow mode on; it is turned off only after a stated number of shadowed approvals reconcile cleanly against what would have been sent. Toggling it is an audit event.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:216:- Re-authing every Sunday resets the 7-day clock so it never expires mid-week. Caveat: expiry is 7 days from issuance, so the email lands earlier than the prior week's auth time, and a daily health check escalates (Mon, then Tue) if the re-auth hasn't happened. On expiry, sync jobs pause and queue rather than erroring.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:222:  2. Order proposal state machine: every legal and illegal transition (proposed → validated/rejected → approved → submitted → filled/cancelled), plus idempotency (double-submit of the same proposal must be impossible).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:226:- **Playwright** for clickable UI: approval queue flow (approve/reject a proposal, override a stop outside the collar with a logged reason), dashboard renders with seeded data, risk-rule editor. These run against a seeded test DB with a fake Schwab adapter, not cassettes.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:232:A second rule set alongside the trading guardrails, covering the book-level behaviors from post-crash market research (concentration of best days, lump-sum vs staged deployment, threshold rebalancing, correlation breakdown, leveraged-proxy discipline). Kept structurally separate from per-trade guardrails: trading rules judge one order, allocation rules judge the whole book. Both feed the same proposal → approval pipeline; nothing here auto-executes.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:238:1. **Threshold rebalancing.** Nightly drift check against `allocation_targets`. When any weight drifts beyond its band (default 5 percentage points, per-target configurable), the agent generates rebalance proposals (sell overweight, buy underweight) through the normal pipeline with guardrail evaluation. The rule is mechanical; the approval is still human. A minimum trade notional (configurable, e.g., $100) suppresses churn on a small account; drift that would require a sub-minimum order is reported, not proposed. Fractional-share support in the order API is unverified; until confirmed, quantities round down to whole shares.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:239:2. **Leveraged-proxy exception.** Symbols tagged leveraged/amplified are excluded from mechanical rebalance proposals. Drift on those instead triggers a thesis-review task: the proposal renders the original thesis from the journal/watchlist next to current numbers, and the human decides deploy / hold / exit. Encodes "the discipline is the same, the decision is not mechanical."
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:240:3. **Deployment policy for new cash.** Cash inflows (detected via transactions sync) trigger a deployment proposal per the policy John sets in `deployment_policies` (immediate, staged over N weeks, or ask-each-time). The proposal renders the relevant base rates (lump-sum vs staged historical win rates) as context; the policy itself is John's call, stored as data, and changeable only in the rule editor.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:247:**UI:** allocation targets + drift live on the dashboard below positions; rebalance and deployment proposals use the standard Flow-2 proposal detail; thesis-review proposals add the original-thesis panel. Rule authoring goes in the (desktop) rule editor.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:252:**Phase 2 (propose + approve):** guardrail engine, order proposals via MCP, approval UI, bracket submission (entry + child stop, 5.4.2) from UI, ambiguous-outcome reconciliation, settlement checks from broker balances, wash-sale checks against the linked IRA, Hotwire Native iOS app with push and Face ID confirm (5.8a). Ships with shadow mode on.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:253:**Phase 2.5 (allocation module):** targets, drift checks, rebalance/deployment proposals, correlation and cash-drag diagnostics in the Sunday review (§5.12).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:254:**Phase 3 (earned automation):** conditional auto-submit for a narrow class (e.g., pre-approved stop adjustments) only after the journal shows positive expectancy over a real sample; kill-switch; per-day order caps.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:263:- Agent never submits orders; proposal/approval split confirmed.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:269:- Review v8 (Sep 1): real bracket stops at Schwab; local idempotency with reconcile-before-retry; unattended runtime is read-only; trades defined as zero-to-zero lifecycles keyed by CUSIP; shadow mode on by default; broker balances as settled-cash source; market calendar from Schwab; flow-adjusted equity series; min rebalance notional; single-writer memory repo; one append-only audit table.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:279:- **Cash-secured puts:** the engine must reserve settled cash equal to strike × 100 per contract and exclude it from "spendable" in every other proposal's GFV check.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:288:**Tax lots (2a, resolved):** the order object carries a TaxLotMethod field, so per-order lot method selection is possible. Default FIFO for v1; expose the method dropdown on sell proposals. Exact enum values to confirm against official docs post-approval.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:299:- Agent hallucination and prompt injection are contained by design: the agent never computes position size or submits orders, and unattended runs cannot create proposals at all (5.5a).
