docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:18:6. Dashboard with all four banner states (healthy / token expiring / token expired / halted). Halted can be reached via a manual flag in Phase 1 since no guardrails run yet.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:21:9. Shadow mode flag exists and is on (nothing to submit yet, but the flag, the audit event, and the UI indicator ship now).
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:24:Not in Phase 1: guardrail engine, proposals, approval UI, order submission, bracket stops, allocation module, FMP. Do not scaffold them beyond the migrations.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:32:- **Every "logged" action is an `audit_events` row.** Re-auth, token refresh failures, shadow-mode toggles, manual halt flag.
docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md:33:- Schwab account access is approved and the app is registered (status pending Ready For Use). Production host is a dokku app on GC2 at `desk.athayde.com`; callback is `https://desk.athayde.com/schwab/callback`; `SCHWAB_APP_KEY`, `SCHWAB_APP_SECRET`, and `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL` already exist as dokku config vars, so read exactly those names from ENV. Build the client against the schwab-py order-builder docs and community client libraries for response shapes; isolate every Schwab-shape assumption in the adapter layer so official schemas can replace them without touching callers. The live OAuth test waits on Ready For Use; everything else does not.
