app/models/guardrails.rb:1:# The guardrail engine (docs/phase-2-plan.md §3): rules as data, evaluated in Rails against every proposal,
app/models/guardrails.rb:2:# never bypassed or edited through a tool. Evaluation answers; the writers (evaluate!, the approve path) act.
app/models/guardrails.rb:6:  # One rule's verdict. overridable: a caution the approver may pass with a logged reason (today, only the
app/models/guardrails.rb:7:  # collar). trip: a rule halt this verdict asks the writer to engage, with its reset time (nil = until cleared).
app/models/guardrails.rb:17:  # What one evaluation said, in the shape the proposal stores and the detail page reads.
app/models/guardrails.rb:21:    def needs_override? = results.any? { |r| r.caution? && r.overridable }
app/models/guardrails.rb:26:  # The one place a report changes the desk: the halts its rules asked for, engaged by the writer that owns the transaction.
app/models/guardrails.rb:27:  def self.engage_halts!(report, settings: SystemSettings.instance)
app/models/guardrails.rb:28:    report.trips.each { |trip| settings.trip_rule_halt!(rule: trip[:rule], reason: trip[:reason], resets_at: trip[:resets_at]) }
