docs/phase-1-plan.md:36:| 9 | `submission_attempts` | `order_proposal_id`, `attempted_at`, `payload` jsonb, `response` jsonb, `outcome` enum (submitted, unknown, failed, reconciled), `reconciled_order_id` (nullable) | no |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:72:| `Sync::PositionsJob(account)` | via tick | `/accounts/{hash}?fields=positions`; resolve instruments (§2 "Instrument identity"); upsert positions; append a `balances` row; delete positions absent from the response only when the run is complete (every position resolved) and the payload is sane (no positions with positive long market value is a `failed` run, not an empty account); then `Journal::BootstrapJob` for trading-enabled accounts |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:203:- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to` (25-minute refresh, 7-day expiry unaffected by refreshes, pause and catch-up, Mon/Tue escalation rule); sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions incl. removal, orders incl. cancel/replace and working stops, transactions incl. cash dividend, split, return of capital, CUSIP succession, fee items); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill, sell-first legacy holding, bootstrap, ticker change on same CUSIP, R math); snapshot math (flows, late-landing deposit rebuild); MCP tool contracts (auth, each tool's schema and output, permission metadata excludes non-scheduled tools); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (turn cap, degraded mode).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:205:- **`Schwab::FakeClient`** implements the same interface as `Schwab::Client`, returns canned payloads, selected by `config.x.schwab.adapter`. Used by dev seeds and Playwright.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:258:- `/accounts/{hash}?fields=positions` returns balances in the same payload (`currentBalances`, `initialBalances`).
docs/phase-2-plan.md:8:2. **Shadow mode stays on for the whole phase.** `SystemSettings#shadow_mode` is true by default; turning it off is a typed-confirmation toggle on the system page, audited (`shadow_mode_toggled`). In shadow mode the approve path runs end to end and the submission step audits `would_have_submitted` with the exact payload instead of calling Schwab; the proposal leaves the approvable states exactly as a real submission would. **Shadow reconciliation is defined:** the operator places the shadowed order by hand at Schwab, the sync ingests it as `schwab_direct`, and the same matcher the reconcile job uses (§5) links the `would_have_submitted` attempt to that order and diffs the payload against the shape Schwab returned. The system page counts shadowed approvals and how many reconciled cleanly; that count, not a number in this plan, is what the operator reads before turning shadow off. This exercises the matcher and the bracket shape before either guards money.
docs/phase-2-plan.md:9:3. **Two halts, not one.** The kill switch (Phase 1's manual halt, Flow 8) stops everything: entries, exits, stop adjustments, tool proposals. A rule halt (daily loss, max drawdown; PRD §5.4 3) blocks new entries only; exits and tighten-only stop adjustments stay available. Rule halts are durable state on `system_settings` (`rule_halt_rule`, `rule_halt_reason`, `rule_halt_tripped_at`, `rule_halt_resets_at`), tripped by the evaluator or the nightly check with one `rule_halt_tripped` audit and one email, cleared at the reset time or by the operator with a reason. `SystemSettings#writes_allowed?` is replaced by `entries_allowed?` (no kill switch, no rule halt) and `exits_allowed?` (no kill switch); shadow mode is not a gate but the branch between `would_have_submitted` and a real call.
docs/phase-2-plan.md:12:6. **Idempotency is local (PRD §5.1) and survives a killed worker.** Two transactions, not one. First: lock the proposal row, verify the state and the gates, re-evaluate, move `validated → submitting`, insert the `submission_attempts` row with the payload, commit. Then the HTTP call with short explicit timeouts (5 s open, 20 s read, no retries). Second: record the outcome. Nothing re-enters an approvable state from `submitting` or `submission_unknown`. A `submitting` row older than the timeouts plus slack is swept to `submission_unknown` by the tick, never back. A 2xx without a parsable order id is `submission_unknown`. The broker order id goes on the proposal in the second transaction; the orders sync links the order and its child by that id, since Schwab carries no proposal id. Database invariants: at most one attempt per proposal whose outcome is not `failed` (partial unique index); `submitted` requires an attempt; `filled` and `cancelled` are written only by the sync.
docs/phase-2-plan.md:22:16. **Every state change is an audit event** with the actor: `proposal_created`, `proposal_evaluated`, `proposal_approved` (acknowledged warnings, override reason), `proposal_rejected`, `proposal_submitting`, `proposal_submitted`, `would_have_submitted`, `submission_unknown`, `submission_reconciled`, `submission_failed`, `proposal_expired`, `proposal_filled`, `proposal_cancelled`, `rule_changed` (before and after), `rule_halt_tripped`, `rule_halt_cleared`, `shadow_mode_toggled`, `unprotected_alert_sent`, `agent_tool_used` (written after the call, with the outcome and the tool_calls id).
docs/phase-2-plan.md:29:| `submission_attempts` (exists) | `outcome` enum: `pending` (transaction one wrote it, the call has not answered), `submitted`, `would_have_submitted`, `unknown`, `not_placed`, `failed`; partial unique index on `order_proposal_id` where outcome not in (`failed`, `not_placed`); `broker_order_id`, `reconciled_at`. "A `submitted` proposal has an attempt" is a model invariant (the transitions write both in one transaction), not a database constraint |
docs/phase-2-plan.md:80:3. Proposals end to end in shadow: `Proposals::Create`, `propose_order`, the manual form, the queue and detail, `approve_and_submit!` with the two transactions, the payload builder, `would_have_submitted`, the shadow reconciliation matcher and count, expiry, rejection.
app/jobs/sync/positions_job.rb:3:  # position resolved and the payload is sane. Zero-quantity positions are treated as absent.
docs/verify-on-approval.md:77:50. Whether the order POST answers 201 with the new order id in the `Location` header, and what a duplicate or rejected payload answers.
docs/verify-on-approval.md:84:57. Whether `previewOrder` exists on the individual tier, so the payload builder can be checked without an order.
docs/phase-2-state-table.md:14:| `submitting` | shadow branch (system) | `submitted` (shadow), attempt `would_have_submitted` | `would_have_submitted` | the operator places it by hand; the matcher links the Schwab-direct order later (`submission_reconciled`) |
docs/phase-2-state-table.md:27:Invariants the database enforces: one attempt per proposal whose outcome is not `failed` or `not_placed` (partial unique index); one proposal per account and instrument in `submitting` or `submission_unknown` (partial unique index); `broker_order_id` unique among proposals when present. Attempt outcomes: `pending` (transaction one wrote it and the call has not answered; it is what holds the index between the two transactions), `submitted`, `would_have_submitted`, `unknown`, `not_placed`, `failed`. "A `submitted` proposal has an attempt" is a model invariant kept by the transitions, which write both in one transaction, not a database constraint.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:110:Push (deep-link only, no figures in the payload): new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, unprotected position, token expiring. Email: morning brief, EOD summary, Sunday ritual, job-failure digests. Original list:
spec/models/order_proposal_matrix_spec.rb:32:    when :start_submission then proposal.start_submission!(user: john, acknowledged: [], override_reason: nil, payload: {}, shadow: true)
spec/models/order_proposal_matrix_spec.rb:69:    expect { stale.start_submission!(user: john, acknowledged: [], override_reason: nil, payload: {}, shadow: true) }.to raise_error(OrderProposal::IllegalTransition)
spec/models/order_proposal_matrix_spec.rb:77:    expect { second.start_submission!(user: john, acknowledged: [], override_reason: nil, payload: {}, shadow: true) }.to raise_error(OrderProposal::IllegalTransition, /still unresolved/)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:197:- **Notifications, revised:** time-sensitive alerts move from email to push once the app exists: new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, `unprotected` position, token expiring. Briefs and the Sunday ritual stay email (long-form, read on a desktop anyway). Push payloads carry no financial figures; they deep-link and the app fetches.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:209:- **Shadow mode (Schwab has no sandbox):** a global flag, on by default in production until deliberately turned off. In shadow mode the entire pipeline runs, including human approval, but the submission step writes a `would_have_submitted` audit event and the order payload instead of calling Schwab. Playwright runs in shadow mode. Phase 2 ships with shadow mode on; it is turned off only after a stated number of shadowed approvals reconcile cleanly against what would have been sent. Toggling it is an audit event.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:225:  5. Sync jobs: fixture payloads for positions/transactions, including corporate-action and dividend events, verifying journal linking.
